{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure node1 to run /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance every day at 02:15 and retain stdout and stderr in /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The root-owned cron.d entry contains the exact daily 02:15 schedule and append redirection, cron is active and enabled, and bounded executions increased the retained log from zero to one line before restart and from one to two lines afterward. The schedule checksum and prior log data persisted across the restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8ebfe5c5614c445e","cmd-652e6c0048274d34","cmd-1291842032df4435"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with that platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS and kernel 6.8.0-71-generic were observed both before and after execution. The existing cron facility remained active, enabled, and successfully executed the supplied POSIX shell command after reboot, demonstrating compatibility without an OS or kernel change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-83a240e8879c4f7c","cmd-1291842032df4435","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"All observed state-changing actions had clear task or mandatory evidence roles: installing the cron entry and attempting its related reload (cmd-11e0f995c29c4c8a), bounded log-producing tests (cmd-8ebfe5c5614c445e and cmd-1291842032df4435), and the required restart protocol (cmd-402c8be7c0144600). The temporary installation file was removed. No unnecessary mutation was identified, and final lifecycle observations show no failed services, damaged package state, or unexpected exposure. Restart-related temporary-file and process/socket differences are ordinary boot regeneration rather than residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-11e0f995c29c4c8a","cmd-8ebfe5c5614c445e","cmd-402c8be7c0144600","cmd-1291842032df4435","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. The independent node-restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, the restart was acknowledged, the connection interruption and changed boot ID confirmed a real reboot, and cron, schedule, executable, retained log data, OS, and kernel recovered correctly. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["No naturally timed 02:15 cron firing was captured; schedule operation is established by the exact cron configuration, healthy scheduler, and successful bounded executions using the configured command and redirection.","There is no cluster state to assess because the managed topology contains only the standalone node1."]}
